      "writtenOn": "2020-04-01T22:16:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is validating the internal workings of the state machine.\n\nWe could change the number of state and sub-states and it shouldn\u0027t matter as long as the contract (in terms of timing and resistors changing) still holds true.\n\nThe impl should be free to express its state machine how ever it likes.",
      "parentUuid": "ff3026b8_4d3adc29",
      "revId": "8f9a4f8720dc64e5df9423c9d2d3543770f16595",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db20e3de_11e4d2d9",
        "filename": "test/usb_typec_drp_acc_trysrc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 555,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-01T23:49:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The states are externally defined by the PD spec, not just an internal implementation detail, that\u0027s one of the things I like about TCPMv2, so we are checking we have implemented the spec correctly, which seems like a good thing to me.\n\nIf you really don\u0027t want the direct connection, then how about a mapping from internal state to external PD spec state to decouple them? Then do something like:\nTEST_ASSERT(pd_spec_state(PORT0) \u003d\u003d PD_SPEC_ATTACH_WAIT_SNK)\n\nI feel like not having any access to the state makes it more inconvenient and error prone to write tests, which will lead to fewer tests.",
      "parentUuid": "90d3828d_3bb6782a",
      "revId": "8f9a4f8720dc64e5df9423c9d2d3543770f16595",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3eab173b_4397091c",
        "filename": "test/usb_typec_drp_acc_trysrc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 555,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-02T04:40:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see the temptation to verify spec states, but I tend to agree with Jett that it\u0027s the external factors which should ultimately be tested.  I\u0027d like for us to follow the same philosophy when we do more PE testing: testing the messages in and out more so than the states themselves.  Some of the reasoning is that we don\u0027t always follow the spec states (ex. auto toggle and low power mode are top of mind), and some is that it\u0027s ultimately the external behavior that matters in practice.\n\nI also miss our desk clump conversations about things like this.",
      "parentUuid": "db20e3de_11e4d2d9",
      "revId": "8f9a4f8720dc64e5df9423c9d2d3543770f16595",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56d9325d_7dab14f7",
        "filename": "test/usb_typec_drp_acc_trysrc.c",
